EEMBC harness over the Verilator RTL (VM harness test)
======================================================

Runs the real EEMBC th_lite benchmark (bmark_lite.c: timing + per-word golden
check + CRC-vs-EXPECTED_CRC) with the decode loop driven by the Verilator
viterbi_accelerator RTL instead of the software decoder (built with
-DUSE_HW_ACCEL). This is the only test path kept here: the EEMBC harness
scoring hardware-produced output.

Requires Verilator, so run it on the VM where Verilator is installed.

Run (from this directory):

    ./build_bench_hw_vm.sh [DATA]

      DATA  dataset: 1 = gett (default)  2 = toggle  3 = ones  4 = zeros

e.g. all four:

    ./build_bench_hw_vm.sh 1
    ./build_bench_hw_vm.sh 2
    ./build_bench_hw_vm.sh 3
    ./build_bench_hw_vm.sh 4

Each run prints the harness verdict (DONE / Failure) and the CRC. A pass means
the CRC matches EXPECTED_CRC in bmark_lite.c:
    gett   0x79f0   toggle 0x096a   ones 0x48bf   zeros 0x0000
gett/toggle are checked against the *_golden_hamming.dat references (the
hard-decision Hamming output the RTL produces); ones/zeros use the stock
goldens.

What the script does (see the header comment in build_bench_hw_vm.sh for the
full file list needed on the VM):
    [1] verilate the RTL  ->  obj_dir/Vviterbi_accelerator__ALL.a
                              (skipped if already built; rm -rf obj_dir to force)
    [2] compile the benchmark + th_lite harness C sources
    [3] compile hw_driver.cpp + collect the Verilator runtime
    [4] link (g++ -pthread) -> build/viterbi_bench_hw, then run it

Notes:
  - th_lite/ and telecom/ live OUTSIDE this git repo, so they are not pulled in
    by cloning it; they must be present on the VM (the script checks and the
    header comment lists exactly which files).
  - Build artifacts land in build/ and obj_dir/ under this directory; nothing
    is written back into the th_lite/ or telecom/ trees.
